  "scene": {
    "id": "distribute",
    "language": "Okay, so as the midfielder, you should always pass. Well, there are some things that you should consider. You should, if possible, you should pass to the deepest option, which is the right striker over there. If the right striker is not open, you should either hold position or, like, play with your left winger. But in this scenario, the right striker is open right now, so what I'm gonna do [0]is I'm gonna pass... As a midfielder, I'm gonna pass to this right striker [1]and then, the right striker now has[2] the ball. I'm gonna make a run into space to provide some support. The right striker now has some options. He has me, he has his left striker, and his left winger is most likely gonna make a run, so... And there are only two defenders, so it's a 3v2, so he can either pass it to me here and make a run. He could pass it to me and I can take a shot. And yeah, that would be... He can play with his left striker, pass it to his left striker, and then both the right striker and me would make a run and yeah, that would be the best play here.",
